.TH SHOAL-LSP 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal-lsp \- provide language-server features for Shoal source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal-lsp
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the Language Server Protocol over standard input and standard output for editor integrations.
The transport admits bounded framed input and supports diagnostics, completion, hover,
navigation, symbols, and safe formatting responses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print help and exit without starting the protocol transport.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Writes only Language Server Protocol frames to standard output while serving.
Transport errors are written to standard error after the session closes.
.SH ERRORS
Unexpected command-line arguments return a usage error.
Malformed or oversized framed input closes the affected protocol session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
shoal-lsp
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 after an orderly protocol shutdown and 2 for invalid command-line arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal (1)
